INT. ARJUN'S HOUSE - DAY

Arjun packs a small bag. A photograph of Ravi leans against the mirror.

ARJUN
(quietly)
Ten years is a long time to be gone.

EXT. STREET - DAY

The rain has stopped. Puddles hold the neon of a closed pharmacy.

EXT. LEVEL CROSSING - DAWN

A freight train rolls past. Maya waits behind the barrier with a red umbrella.

MAYA
You are late, Arjun.

INT. OLD RAILWAY STATION - DAY

Arjun walks the empty platform. A clock above him has stopped at 4:10.

INT. POLICE STATION - NIGHT

Arjun enters carrying a pistol. Rain drips from his coat.

He places the RED FOLDER on the desk.

MEERA
You said you would never come back.

ARJUN
(quietly)
Neither did the folder.

EXT. OLD RAILWAY STATION - NIGHT

Ravi crosses the tracks and does not look back.

INT. MORGUE - MORNING

Meera reads a tag on a cold steel drawer.

MEERA
Same hands. Same knot.

INT. RAVI'S HOUSE - NIGHT

Ravi lights one candle. The power is out across the street.

RAVI
Dad? Is that you?

EXT. HOSPITAL - DAY

An ambulance backs into the bay. Maya runs beside the stretcher.

INT. HOSPITAL CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Arjun sits alone under a flickering tube light.

MAYA
He is asking for you.

EXT. STREET - NIGHT

Rain again. Meera follows a red motorcycle at a distance.

INT. POLICE STATION - DAY

Meera pins a photograph to the board. The RED FOLDER is open in front of her.

MEERA
(to herself)
Where is the last page?
